00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>I am no longer Mattis' child.</i>

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.120
<i>So, I have to go.</i>

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.280
After four days, she found Birk,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.470
who planned to leave Borka's Keep and move into the forest.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:49.870
Upon learning that, Ronja decided to leave the castle.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:54.320
In the middle of the night, Ronja quietly bid her mother farewell,

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.130
venturing through the forest to meet Birk at the Bear's Cave.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.010
What Lurks Within The Cave

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.010
What Lurks Within The Cave

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.320
Plagued by thoughts of Mattis' Castle, Ronja couldn't fall asleep.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.420
"It's the same sky over Mattis' fort."

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:46.700
"The same river rushing by that I can hear at home."

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.760
After thinking such thoughts, Ronja was finally able to drift off.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.380
I'm blue with cold!

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.770
But dawn is the coldest hour,

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.290
then it gets warmer bit by bit.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.300
Isn't it a comfort to know that?

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.680
A fire would still be more comfortable.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.120
Here.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.610
From now on we'll be drinking spring water, and nothing else.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.640
It won't make us fat.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.120
But we won't die of it either.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:46.990
Ronja!

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.920
Do you know?

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.120
We can afford to roar with laughter...

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.390
We are free!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.530
Yes!

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:39.200
This is our kingdom!

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:48.180
No one can take it away from us,

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.620
or drive us out!

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.330
Cover your ears.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.120
My spring yell is coming!

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.670
I've forgotten something important.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:59.610
I need to fetch my crossbow before you bring the wild harpies down on us with your yelling.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:04.190
Fetch? From where? From Borka's Keep?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.860
No, from the woods outside of it.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.780
I'm hiding my luggage about there.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:17.120
I had too many things to bring them all up with me at once.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.480
I'm hiding my crossbow there, too.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.720
Mattis didn't want me to have a crossbow yet.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.970
But I can cut myself an ordinary bow,

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:35.260
if I can borrow your knife!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.000
Sure thing!

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.400
Just be careful not to lose it.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:47.840
It's the most precious thing we have.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.270
Without a knife, we can't manage in the woods.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.490
Remember that.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:00.990
There are other things we can't manage without.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:06.450
For example, the bucket to draw water.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.530
Have you considered that?

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.170
Of course I've considered that.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.340
But we can't draw water just by thinking about it.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:22.010
Then I guess it's a good thing that I know just where to get one.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.010
Where?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.840
By Lovis' healing spring.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.960
Below the Wolf's Neck.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.600
In the woods.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:06.410
Sturkus left a bucket behind when he left there in a hurry yesterday.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.720
She sent Sturkus there for the healing water for Skalle-Per,

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.820
which he needs to drink for his stomach problems.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:20.520
Sturkus will have to go back there to get the bucket today.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.330
Lovis will see to that, believe me.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.330
So, if we go there beforehand...

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:32.580
Yeah. We can bring the bucket back.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:33.900
Uh-huh.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:40.970
Let's go!

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.090
Yup.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:28.910
All right!

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.450
Wow!

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:45.570
Yes, I see you know what we woodsman have to do.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.020
This proves that!

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.180
We'll get our food by ourselves from now on,

00:10:54.180 --> 00:11:00.290
and we'll protect ourselves from violent wild harpies and scary beasts.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:05.580
I know that well enough.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:11.540
If it's you and me, I'm sure we can—

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.360
Quiet.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.850
There's someone inside the cave.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.320
Come out, harpies!

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:54.480
If you want to meet the sharpest spear in these woods!

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:07.740
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:07.740
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:24.800
Human here...

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:28.300
Gray dwarves all...

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:32.240
Bite and strike...

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.660
They're good swimmers, those little buggers.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:57.260
And good bread eaters too.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.470
Oh my...

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:13.530
This bread wasn't chewed up.

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:18.620
I'm surprised they left this big loaf intact...

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.160
This is not good at all.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.540
The whole of this forest will be in a fuss

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.810
with them chattering that "shoo shoo, shii shii" nonsense.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.010
If so...

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:37.690
Every last harpy will know where we are soon.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.510
But you are not allowed to be afraid in Mattis' forest!

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.480
I've been taught that since I was a child!

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:57.660
And it's stupid to live in dread of something that hasn't even happened yet.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.840
Yeah, that's right!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:06.000
Be calm, and figure out what we have and what we need.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:12.540
Yeah, and we should collect what we don't have from the forest, right?

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.700
Hey!

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:50.870
Hey, Birk.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.160
Tomorrow I'll...

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.440
Huh?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:28.430
Birk, I'll cut some new arrows tomorrow.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:33.430
Okay. Just be careful not to lose the knife.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:41.140
Yes I know, it's the most precious thing we have.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.370
The knife, and the ax.

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:59.290
<i>Wolves, wolves...</i>

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:59.290
<i>Wolves, wolves...</i>

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:04.610
<i>Howl in the forest late at night</i>

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:04.610
<i>Howl in the forest late at night</i>

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:13.200
<i>They howl and wail in their sleeplessness</i>

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:13.200
<i>They howl and wail in their sleeplessness</i>

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:18.760
Hey, Birk.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:24.320
Do you think they're thinking about us in Mattis' fort?

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:25.890
I mean...

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.570
Our parents, that is.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:44.590
It would be odd if they weren't.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:49.390
Is everyone feeling sad about us?

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:54.680
That's different for each person, I think.

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:59.970
My mother will be sad, but she'll get angry more than that.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:06.780
And my father will get angry, but he'll be more sad at the same time.

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:10.260
My mother is feeling sad.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.370
I know that.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.180
What about Mattis?

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:24.960
I should think he's feeling relieved.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.130
Now that I've gone, he can forget me.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:54.790
That night, Ronja had a dream...

